INT. SHIPBOARD OPERATING THEATRE - NIGHT

A hospital ship in mid-ocean. Steel walls, bolted tables, lamps swaying in their housings. The deck rolls with a slow rhythm. Water drips from an unseen pipe.

The theatre is empty. Instruments laid out in perfect rows. A digital recorder rests on the scrub sink, its red light blinking.

The door swings open. A woman steps through: DR. SAOIRSE KELLEHER-MBEKI (40s, blue scrubs soaked at the collar, surgical cap, eyes red from forty hours awake). She carries a paper cup of tea and a patient file.

She sets the cup down. Looks at the empty table.

SAOIRSE
Nobody. Good.

She picks up the recorder. Presses play. Her own voice fills the room, taped hours earlier.

SAOIRSE (V.O.)
(recording)
Patient Adebayo. Male, fifty-two. Perforated bowel. We began at nineteen hundred.

Saoirse stops the recording. Rewinds. Plays again.

SAOIRSE (V.O.) (CONT'D)
(recording)
Complication at twenty-one-forty. Hemorrhage. We called it at twenty-two-ten.

She snaps it off. Her hand trembles. She sits on the edge of the table, hard.

SAOIRSE
(softly)
Twenty-two-ten.

She lifts the tea and sips. Grimaces. It's cold. She sips again anyway.

The ship pitches. The tea slides off the sink and spills across the floor. She does not move.

SAOIRSE (CONT'D)
(to the empty room)
I did everything right.

No answer. Water drips.

She stands, crosses to the instrument tray, and lifts a scalpel. Turns it in the light. Sets it down. Picks up the recorder again.

SAOIRSE (CONT'D)
(into recorder)
Dictation. Adebayo, continued. Cause of death: acute hemorrhage secondary to--

Her voice catches. She presses stop. Closes her eyes.

She keeps speaking to the empty theatre.

SAOIRSE (CONT'D)
(whispering)
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

She pulls a grey ship's blanket from a shelf and drapes it over her shoulders. Presses the recorder to her chest.

SAOIRSE (V.O.) (CONT'D)
(recording, from earlier)
Time of death, twenty-two-ten. Closing.

She opens her eyes. Sets the recorder in its cradle, light still blinking, and sits in the dark alone.
